@*
    The reader's pace: how many story points a week an imported plan with no due
    date is drawn at (ADR 0013, ruling 4).

    Four paces, one of them chosen. The one the reader types, and three measured
    from the estimated work they finished over the last two, four and eight weeks,
    each shown with its figure so the reader can see what they are choosing. A
    stretch that finished nothing estimated measured no pace and is not offered at
    all, since there is nothing to place by; with none measured there is no choice
    to offer and only the field is drawn. A line under the choices says so when a
    choice that has since gone empty is placing by the typed pace instead, because
    its button is gone.

    Kept per repository band, because productivity differs from one project to the
    next (ADR 0013, ruling 4 as amended on 2026-09-26), and each pace sits under its
    band's name in the chart's sidebar, above the band's named lanes, where the plans
    it places are drawn. A repository's band carries that repository's pace (Repository set), measured over
    its own finished work. The unfiled band carries the default pace (Repository
    unset), measured over all of it: the one a plan filed in no repository is
    placed at, and the one every repository nobody has set a pace for reads.

    It lives on the roadmap rather than the settings screen because it is read here:
    the figure only decides how long a bar is drawn, and the reader deciding between
    their own guess and what they actually did wants to see both beside the chart.
    A change here that alters the pace this control shows is reported through
    OnPaceChanged, and the band re-lengthens every bar still sized by its effort,
    each at its own repository's pace (ADR 0013, ruling 5 as amended). Finished work
    moving a measured figure is not a change anybody made, so it redraws the figures
    and moves no bar.
*@
@* For @onchange: without it the directive is a plain attribute and never fires. *@
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@implements IDisposable
@inject IPlanningPace Pace
@inject IRoadmapWorkChanges WorkChanges

<div class="roadmap-pace" data-testid="@TestIdOf(null)">
    @* Committed on change rather than bound, so a half-typed pace never reaches the
       store: "2." on the way to "2.5" is not a number. min and step are affordances
       only — the store is the one gate, and refuses the 0 this min still allows. *@
    <div class="roadmap-pace__line">
        <TextField Compact="true"
                   Type="number"
                   AriaLabel="@ManualLabel"
                   CssClass="roadmap-pace__manual"
                   TestId="@TestIdOf("manual")"
                   min="0"
                   step="1"
                   autocomplete="off"
                   Value="@_draft"
                   @onchange="ApplyManual" />
        <span class="roadmap-pace__unit" aria-hidden="true">pt/wk</span>
    </div>

    @* Only the stretches that measured something, each with its figure: one that
       finished nothing has no pace to place by, so it is not offered at all. With
       none of them, "Mine" would be a choice between one thing, so there is no
       group — the field is the pace. *@
    @if (HasMeasured)
    {
        <ButtonGroup CssClass="roadmap-pace__options"
                     AriaLabel="@OptionsLabel"
                     TestId="@TestIdOf("options")">
            @foreach (var option in Options)
            {
                var value = _paces.Of(option.Source);
                if (value is null) continue;

                <ToggleButton BaseClass="btn btn--toggle btn--small"
                              Pressed="@(_paces.Source == option.Source)"
                              Title="@option.Title(value, Repository)"
                              OnClick="() => Choose(option.Source)"
                              TestId="@TestIdOf(option.Key)">
                    <span class="roadmap-pace__option-name">@option.Name</span>
                    @if (option.Source != PaceSource.Manual)
                    {
                        <span class="roadmap-pace__option-value">@Rounded(value.Value)</span>
                    }
                </ToggleButton>
            }
        </ButtonGroup>
    }

    @* One short line, always the same height, so the band never has to grow for
       it. The whole sentence is its title and what a screen reader hears. *@
    @if (Note is { } note)
    {
        <span class="roadmap-pace__note"
              role="status"
              title="@note.Sentence"
              data-testid="@TestIdOf(note.Kind)">
            <span aria-hidden="true">@note.Short</span>
            <span class="sr-only">@note.Sentence</span>
        </span>
    }
</div>

@code {
    private sealed record Option(PaceSource Source, string Key, string Name, string Stretch)
    {
        public string Title(decimal? value, string? repository)
        {
            var plans = repository is null ? "plans in no repository" : $"{repository}'s plans";
            var finished = repository is null ? "what you finished" : $"what you finished in {repository}";

            return Source == PaceSource.Manual || value is not { } measured
                ? $"Place {plans} by the pace you typed"
                : $"Place {plans} by {finished} over the {Stretch}: {Rounded(measured)} points a week";
        }
    }

    /// <summary>What the line under the choices says: a short form to show and the
    /// sentence it stands for.</summary>
    private sealed record PaceNote(string Kind, string Short, string Sentence);

    private static readonly Option[] Options =
    [
        new(PaceSource.Manual, "manual-option", "Mine", "pace you typed"),
        new(PaceSource.LastTwoWeeks, "two-weeks", "2 wk", "last two weeks"),
        new(PaceSource.LastFourWeeks, "four-weeks", "4 wk", "last four weeks"),
        new(PaceSource.LastEightWeeks, "eight-weeks", "8 wk", "last eight weeks")
    ];

    /// <summary>The repository whose pace this is, by alias; unset for the default
    /// pace — the one a plan filed in no repository is placed at, and the one a
    /// repository nobody set a pace for reads.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Repository { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Raised after the reader changed the pace placement uses for this
    /// control's scope — typed a new one while it is in use, or chose another — so
    /// the band can re-lengthen the bars sized by it. Not raised for a refusal, or
    /// for a change that leaves the pace in use where it was.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnPaceChanged { get; set; }

    private PlanningPacesDto _paces = new(7m, null, null, null, PaceSource.Manual);
    private string _draft = string.Empty;
    private string? _error;
    private string? _read;
    private bool _initialized;

    private string ManualLabel => Repository is null
        ? "Default points a week, for plans in no repository and repositories without a pace of their own"
        : $"Points a week for {Repository}";

    private string OptionsLabel => Repository is null
        ? "Which default pace places a plan"
        : $"Which pace places a plan in {Repository}";

    private string Where => Repository is null ? string.Empty : $" in {Repository}";

    /// <summary>Whether any stretch measured something — and so whether there is a
    /// choice to offer at all.</summary>
    private bool HasMeasured =>
        _paces.LastTwoWeeks is not null || _paces.LastFourWeeks is not null || _paces.LastEightWeeks is not null;

    /// <summary>What the line under the choices says, most pressing first: a refused
    /// figure, since it is what the reader just did; then a chosen stretch that has
    /// since measured nothing — its button is gone, so this is the only place left
    /// that says the typed pace is placing instead. A stretch that measured nothing
    /// needs no line: its missing button says it.</summary>
    private PaceNote? Note
    {
        get
        {
            if (_error is not null) return new PaceNote("refused", "Not saved — see why", _error);

            if (_paces.FellBack)
            {
                return new PaceNote(
                    "fell-back",
                    "Empty stretch: using Mine",
                    $"Nothing estimated was finished{Where} in that stretch, so the pace you typed is used.");
            }

            return null;
        }
    }

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        Pace.Changed += OnChanged;
        WorkChanges.Changed += OnChanged;
        await Read();
        _initialized = true;
    }

    /// <summary>A control handed another repository reads that one's pace.</summary>
    protected override async Task OnParametersSetAsync()
    {
        if (!_initialized || string.Equals(_read, Repository, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)) return;

        _error = null;
        await Read();
    }

    public void Dispose()
    {
        Pace.Changed -= OnChanged;
        WorkChanges.Changed -= OnChanged;
    }

    private async Task Read()
    {
        _read = Repository;
        _paces = await Pace.ReadAsync(Repository);

        // A refused value stays on screen beside its reason, so the reader can see
        // what they typed; otherwise the field shows what is stored.
        if (_error is null) _draft = Format(_paces.Manual);
    }

    private async Task ApplyManual(ChangeEventArgs e)
    {
        var typed = e.Value?.ToString() ?? string.Empty;
        _draft = typed;
        var before = _paces.InUse;
        _error = Pace.SetManual(typed, Repository);
        await Read();
        await Announce(before);
    }

    private async Task Choose(PaceSource source)
    {
        var before = _paces.InUse;
        _error = Pace.Choose(source, Repository);
        await Read();
        await Announce(before);
    }

    /// <summary>Compared on the pace in use rather than on the setter's answer: a
    /// pace that took but could not be written for next time still answers with a
    /// warning, and a new typed pace while a measured one is chosen moves
    /// nothing.</summary>
    private async Task Announce(decimal before)
    {
        if (_paces.InUse != before) await OnPaceChanged.InvokeAsync();
    }

    // Raised from whatever thread saved the pace or wrote a task.
    private void OnChanged() => _ = InvokeAsync(async () =>
    {
        await Read();
        StateHasChanged();
    });

    /// <summary>Every test id carries the scope at the end — the repository, or
    /// "default" — so each band's control can be told apart.</summary>
    private string TestIdOf(string? part)
    {
        var id = part is null ? "roadmap-pace" : $"roadmap-pace-{part}";
        return $"{id}-{(Repository is null ? "default" : Slug(Repository))}";
    }

    private static string Slug(string value) =>
        new([.. value.Select(character => char.IsLetterOrDigit(character) ? char.ToLowerInvariant(character) : '-')]);

    /// <summary>Four decimals, no trailing zeroes, invariant — how the store writes
    /// a pace, so a committed value reads back spelled the way it was kept.</summary>
    private static string Format(decimal pace) => pace.ToString("0.####", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);

    /// <summary>A measured pace to two decimals for reading at a glance. Placement
    /// still divides by the four it was measured to.</summary>
    private static string Rounded(decimal pace) => pace.ToString("0.##", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);
}
